---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

// Texto proporcionado por Daniel (Privacy_Policy.docx), sin cambios.
const lastUpdated = "September 2026";
---
<Base
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy Policy for the Daniel Couttolenc Studio website."
  noindex
>
  <article class="legal">
    <h1 class="type-heading">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="legal__updated type-meta">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <p>
      Daniel Couttolenc Diaz Barriga operating under the name Daniel Couttolenc Studio
      (&ldquo;Daniel Couttolenc Studio,&rdquo; &ldquo;we,&rdquo; &ldquo;us,&rdquo; or
      &ldquo;our&rdquo;), is responsible for the processing and protection of personal
      data collected through this website, in accordance with applicable Mexican data
      protection laws.
    </p>

    <section>
      <h2>1. Data Controller</h2>
      <p class="legal__address">
        Name: Daniel Couttolenc Diaz Barriga<br />
        Trade name: Daniel Couttolenc Studio<br />
        Address: Diagonal Rancho San Isidro 3216-A, 304-B. Santiago Momoxpan, San Pedro
        Cholula &mdash; Puebla, Mexico 72775<br />
        Email: <a href="mailto:daniel@danielcouttolenc.com">daniel@danielcouttolenc.com</a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>2. Personal Information We Collect</h2>
      <p>
        When you contact Daniel Couttolenc Studio through the contact form available on
        this website, we may collect the following personal information:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>First name</li>
        <li>Last name</li>
        <li>Email address</li>
        <li>Subject or title of your inquiry</li>
        <li>The content of your message</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We may also process certain technical information associated with a form
        submission, such as the date and time of the submission and information
        generated or processed by the services used to operate the form.
      </p>
      <p>We do not intentionally request or collect sensitive personal data through this website.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>3. How We Collect Your Information</h2>
      <p>Personal information is collected when you voluntarily submit the contact form on this website.</p>
      <p>
        The contact form is operated using Netlify Forms, a service provided by
        Netlify, Inc. Netlify stores form submissions in its database and provides
        tools for managing those submissions.
      </p>
      <p>The website is hosted and deployed through Netlify.</p>
      <p>For more information about Netlify&rsquo;s privacy practices, please refer to its Privacy Statement.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>4. Purposes of Processing</h2>
      <p>Your personal information may be processed for the following purposes:</p>
      <p class="legal__subhead">Primary purposes</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Responding to inquiries and messages submitted through the website.</li>
        <li>Communicating with you regarding pieces, collections, projects, commissions, or services.</li>
        <li>Providing information specifically requested by you.</li>
        <li>Maintaining professional communications resulting from your inquiry.</li>
        <li>Maintaining and operating the website.</li>
        <li>Complying with applicable legal obligations.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="legal__subhead">Secondary purposes</p>
      <p>
        We do not currently use the personal information submitted through the contact
        form for unrelated advertising or marketing purposes.
      </p>
      <p>
        If our practices change in the future, this Privacy Notice will be updated
        and, where required by applicable law, the corresponding consent will be
        obtained.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>5. Use and Disclosure of Personal Information</h2>
      <p>We do not sell or rent your personal information.</p>
      <p>
        Your information may be processed by service providers that are necessary for
        the operation of this website and its contact functionality.
      </p>
      <p>
        In particular, contact form submissions are processed and stored through
        Netlify Forms. Netlify states that form submission data is stored in its
        database and provides functionality for managing and deleting submissions.
      </p>
      <p>
        We will only use or disclose your personal information for the purposes
        described in this Privacy Notice or as otherwise permitted or required by
        applicable law.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>6. Options to Limit the Use or Disclosure of Your Information</h2>
      <p>
        You may request that we limit the use or disclosure of your personal
        information, to the extent applicable under Mexican law.
      </p>
      <p>
        You may submit such a request by contacting us at{" "}
        <a href="mailto:daniel@danielcouttolenc.com">daniel@danielcouttolenc.com</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>7. ARCO Rights</h2>
      <p>Under applicable Mexican law, you have the right to exercise your ARCO rights:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Access:</strong> to know what personal information we hold about you and how it is being processed.</li>
        <li><strong>Rectification:</strong> to request correction of inaccurate or incomplete personal information.</li>
        <li><strong>Cancellation:</strong> to request deletion of your personal information when legally applicable.</li>
        <li><strong>Opposition:</strong> to object to the processing of your personal information in the circumstances provided by law.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="legal__subhead">How to exercise your ARCO rights</p>
      <p>
        You may submit an ARCO request by email to{" "}
        <a href="mailto:daniel@danielcouttolenc.com">daniel@danielcouttolenc.com</a>.
      </p>
      <p>Your request should include:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Your full name.</li>
        <li>A clear description of the personal information concerning which you are exercising your right.</li>
        <li>The specific ARCO right you wish to exercise.</li>
        <li>An email address or other means through which we can communicate our response.</li>
        <li>Documentation reasonably necessary to verify your identity and, where applicable, the authority of your legal representative.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Once your request has been received, we will provide an acknowledgment of
        receipt and process the request in accordance with applicable Mexican law.
      </p>
      <p>
        We will respond to the request within the applicable legal period, which is
        generally 20 business days from receipt of the request. If the request is
        granted, it will generally be made effective within 15 business days following
        notification of the response. These periods may be extended once when legally
        permitted and for justified reasons.
      </p>
      <p>The exercise of ARCO rights is generally free of charge, subject to the applicable legal provisions.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>8. Data Transfers</h2>
      <p>
        Your personal information may be transferred or made available to service
        providers when necessary to operate, maintain, secure, or provide
        functionality for this website.
      </p>
      <p>In particular, contact form submissions are processed through Netlify Forms, operated by Netlify, Inc.</p>
      <p>Where a transfer requires your consent under applicable law, the appropriate consent will be obtained.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>9. Data Security</h2>
      <p>
        We implement reasonable administrative, technical, and physical safeguards
        designed to protect personal information against unauthorized access, use,
        alteration, loss, or disclosure.
      </p>
      <p>However, no method of transmission or electronic storage can be guaranteed to be completely secure.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>10. Data Retention</h2>
      <p>
        Personal information submitted through the contact form will be retained for
        as long as reasonably necessary to respond to your inquiry, maintain the
        resulting professional communication, comply with applicable legal
        obligations, or resolve potential disputes.
      </p>
      <p>We may periodically delete information that is no longer necessary for these purposes.</p>
      <p>
        Netlify provides functionality to permanently delete form submissions, and
        personal information stored through Netlify Forms will be managed and deleted
        when appropriate.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>11. Cookies and Similar Technologies</h2>
      <p>
        This website does not currently use personal information collected through the
        contact form for advertising or unrelated tracking purposes.
      </p>
      <p>
        If analytics, advertising technologies, cookies, or other tracking
        technologies that involve the processing of personal information are
        introduced in the future, this Privacy Notice will be updated as applicable.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>12. Changes to This Privacy Notice</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this Privacy Notice from time to time to reflect changes to our
        website, services, data-processing practices, or applicable legal
        requirements.
      </p>
      <p>
        Any changes will be published on this website, and the date of the most recent
        update will be indicated at the beginning of the Privacy Notice.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>13. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        For questions regarding this Privacy Notice, the processing of your personal
        information, or the exercise of your privacy rights, please contact:
      </p>
      <p class="legal__address">
        Daniel Couttolenc Diaz Barriga<br />
        Daniel Couttolenc Studio<br />
        Diagonal Rancho San Isidro 3216-A, 304-B. Santiago Momoxpan, San Pedro Cholula
        &mdash; Puebla, Mexico 72775<br />
        <a href="mailto:daniel@danielcouttolenc.com">daniel@danielcouttolenc.com</a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <p class="legal__updated type-meta">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .legal {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 40px var(--gutter) 6rem;
  }
  .legal h1 {
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .legal__updated {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 32px;
  }
  .legal > p {
    font-size: var(--fs-body);
    line-height: var(--lh-body);
    margin-bottom: 1em;
  }
  .legal section {
    margin-top: 32px;
  }
  .legal section h2 {
    font-size: var(--fs-body);
    font-weight: var(--fw-medium);
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .legal section p,
  .legal section li {
    font-size: var(--fs-body);
    line-height: var(--lh-body);
  }
  .legal section p + p {
    margin-top: 1em;
  }
  .legal__subhead {
    font-weight: var(--fw-medium);
    margin-top: 1.5em;
  }
  .legal__address {
    font-style: normal;
  }
  .legal section ul {
    margin: 0.75em 0 0;
    padding-left: 1.25em;
  }
  .legal section ul + p {
    margin-top: 1em;
  }
  .legal section li + li {
    margin-top: 0.4em;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .legal {
      padding-top: 24px;
    }
  }
</style>
